<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6d9fd441ec6d7a155fa754d68e8283a5516d68c6" commit="0705e1fbe839e05cc83b2d0363504b737e73d82d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: power_supply: Add types for USB Type C and PD chargers  This adds power supply types for USB chargers defined in the USB Type-C Specification 1.1 and in the USB Power Delivery Specification Revision 2.0 V1.1.  The following are added : POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB_TYPE_C, /* Type C Port */ POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB_PD, /* Type C Power Delivery Port */ POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB_PD_DRP, /* Type C PD Dual Role Port */  Signed-off-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45222,chromium:531628 TEST=Attach the system to a plain SDP Type A host. cat /sys/class/power_supply/CROS_USB_PD_CHARGER0/type Check that the return value is 'USB' Attach to a port that supports charging, or a wall wart. Check that the type is 'Mains'  Change-Id: I6d9fd441ec6d7a155fa754d68e8283a5516d68c6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304660 Commit-Ready: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304660" owner_email="bleung@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/60/304660/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I44395d8af4723cad0f7fb12a0114810109140ca5" commit="3b31b9112ec2a51bd93d6ac77b5ce84ff2f2ddf6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: cros_usbpd-charger - Use new PD and Type C types  Lets map to the new PD and Type C types so we can better inform userspace about the type of power connection we've got.  Since we are now able to express when the other party can supply power (using type USB_PD_DRP), we can also remove the behavior where we would set psy_status= POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING, but set psy_online=1. (see crosbug.com/p/45430)  When we are sourcing power now to another USB_PD Dual Role Device, we will set the type to USB_PD_DRP.  Also, this change will correctly categorize SDP and VBUS modes as POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB, as there is no longer a need for overloaded types.  Signed-off-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45222,chromium:531628,chrome-os-partner:45430 TEST=Attach the system to a plain SDP Type A host. cat /sys/class/power_supply/CROS_USB_PD_CHARGER0/type Check that the return value is 'USB' Attach to a port that supports PD charging such as Zinger. Check that the return value is 'USB_PD' Connect to Samus. Check that the return value is 'USB_PD Dual Role' Finally, check that Guppy and Donnettes return 'USB_C'  Change-Id: I44395d8af4723cad0f7fb12a0114810109140ca5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304661 Commit-Ready: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304661" owner_email="bleung@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/304661/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idea0cc5653167cea4e8c24bd3e1f22fcfa94ffca" commit="4044b6f4f6883c953f741c1f88f9aee72bc2416b" commit_message="power: Leverage new power supply types to determine dual role.  Instead of overloading POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB to mean a dual role USB PD port and POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_MAINS to mean a dedicated port (including anything from a SDP USB port to a high power 60W charger), let's use the new types I've just introduced in crosreview.com/304660 to specifically identify when we are a TYPE_USB_PD_DRP. This also cleans up the logic in detecting a lower power BC 1.2 class USB charger on Yoshi, for example.  Signed-off-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45222,chromium:531628 TEST=Plug a Samus into a Samus. Check that does not charge from other Samus. Check that Zinger still reports as a high power charger. CQ-DEPEND=CL:304661  Change-Id: Idea0cc5653167cea4e8c24bd3e1f22fcfa94ffca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304593 Commit-Ready: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304593" owner_email="bleung@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/93/304593/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I1690a1f39090c57c64d4965092c80eef9070babf" commit="52494ce70369d357f984918eb65242c4bc1e15e0" commit_message="Emile: retrieve the MAC address from vpd  Emile has a on board ethernet.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47465 TEST=vpd -s ethernet_mac0=001122334455      build and check the MAC address  Change-Id: I1690a1f39090c57c64d4965092c80eef9070babf Signed-off-by: ZhengShunQian &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311900 Commit-Ready: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311900" owner_email="zhengsq@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/